      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town began as Morris Station, a whistle‑stop where a small depot and siding shipped lumber and timber.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2,
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://vanishinggeorgia.com/2025/11/11/morris-georgia/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "A post office operated at Morris Station from 1860 until 1950, when the name was shortened to Morris.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        13
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://vanishinggeorgia.com/2025/11/11/morris-georgia/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Georgia General Assembly incorporated Morris as a town in 1911, giving it municipal status for the first time.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        17
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Morris%2C_Georgia",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "In 1995 the town’s municipal charter was repealed, returning Morris to unincorporated status.",
